 forget you know  we've had 10 days of mourning but um  we've got the funeral tomorrow official  national morning ends I think  um day after tomorrow  but  that hasn't brought more money into  people's pockets  people are still going to food banks  during this time  struggling to work out  how to make the budget  last make the pay last as long as the  month  or the benefit last songs of the month  and people are frightened but  I am absolutely that the extraordinary  thing about the Royal Family  is that they knew that  and they are deeply aware of it  and yes there's going to be changes  and the next few months may be very  difficult many many people will be  but from the point of view of the head  of state there's been a seamless  transition  not to someone who's self-centered or  anything like that but as someone who's  sense of service and duty is the equal  of her late majesties  and with the immediate family round and  so though there's not going to be a gap  there there will be the hardship but  there's not going to be the gap  when was the last time you saw her it  was end of June early July  I can't quite remember the exact date  and I went along with um something to  give her actually a a cross of nails  like this these nails are a symbol of  the cathedral they fell from the roof of  the medieval Cathedral as it burned in  the great Blitz it's been used as a  symbol of reconciliation and peace  building around the world and she's had  such an influence on peacemaking and  police building and drawing people  together that I we gave her that gift  and I was privileged to give it to her  I came back and I said to my wife oh  we needn't worry I'm I'm not going to  have to  do a coronation  it'll be my successor who does that  she's so fit  and memory was so acute her observation  so perceptive  you got the benefit of 70 years of  accumulated wisdom in government  and in leadership and you know  not only her family but I think every  senior politician every  Archbishop will will will mess up you  sound like you will have to after that  hugely  you talked about the work the queen did  in peace and conciliation quite frankly  and we will watch all these people  arriving from around the world on Monday  and there is a sense even now that she's  unifying the globe in this don't you  think yes her conciliation and peace  building was not  the sort of Hands-On  way of doing it it was inspirational  and symbolic that made people look at  things a bit differently especially  within the Commonwealth  and work behind the scenes as we know  now from the time of the apartheid  regime in South Africa and  you know being very conscious of the  symbolic importance of what the British  government did at that time for example  um but she's going to unite more global  leaders  possibly than at any point in human  history  um and that is  perhaps a moment I hope and pray that  where they will  reflect on their own leadership  whatever their faith  and they'll be from all faiths and none  um  I hope and pray that they will reflect  on their own leadership and think  do I want my legacy  to be in the bank balance  of Earth  or in the words of Jesus who she  followed so Faithfully do I want to  store up treasure in heaven  and which she has done in her way of  service are you saying that they could  learn from her oh absolutely  um  absolutely I mean there are  extraordinary wonderful leaders coming  um  but I hope they find what they hear and  see and think about  a moment where they say to themselves  I would really like people to look on me  in the way that they look on her  we know they should be buried alongside  her late husband she'll be reunited with  her family her father her mother her  sister her tight knit family did she  really believe that she would see them  again  yes  how did she express that to you  not only to me but in her in that great  covid broadcast but in her Christmas  broadcasts as well  she was a deeply faithful and Faith  filled  under monstrative  quiet  Christian who trusted  in the faithfulness of God  in the words we often use  that she would and her family rest in  peace and rise in glory  it's at the heart of Christian faith  is she at peace now  yes  and should the nation take comfort from  that  I think the nation should take Hope from  that not just comfort  but hope for themselves it's a gift  that she knew that came from God  in whom she believed and trusted in whom  she served and who gave her the strength  to be what she was
 

